From 3435eee3b8aaa5c23fad8e71ab610e8c72b61396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:06:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 885/913] drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: fix res type and unreachable
 resume check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

set_opp stored the TEE_Result returned by regulator_set_voltage in an
int, so an error code overflowed the signed type before being returned.
Use TEE_Result.

In cpu_opp_pm, the resume optimisation only makes sense on STM32MP2,
where the early return covers the Stop1 and LP-Stop1 modes only. On the
other platforms the function already returns early when the RCC clock
tree is not lost, so the same condition can never be true and the check
is dead code. Build it for STM32MP2 only.

Coverity issue: CID 1200188: Overflowed return value in set_opp
Coverity issue: CID 1200630: Logically dead code in cpu_opp_pm

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 0595954a5ead0cfc3ebf622a7d438aa3392ae3ed drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: fix res type and unreachable resume check]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I0b6d142084848be286ada1d258695b9165f3ef4b
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597006
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c b/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
index 02f8ba629..fbab04008 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
@@ -396,7 +396,7 @@ static TEE_Result set_opp(unsigned int opp)
 	unsigned int def_freq_khz = cpu_opp.dvfs[cpu_opp.default_opp].freq_khz;
 	unsigned int opp_freq_khz = cpu_opp.dvfs[opp].freq_khz;
 	int opp_volt_uv = cpu_opp.dvfs[opp].volt_uv;
-	int res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
+	TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
 	struct clk *bypass_parent = NULL;
 
 	if (opp_freq_khz == clk_get_rate(cpu_opp.clock))
@@ -698,6 +698,7 @@ static TEE_Result cpu_opp_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint,
 	if (op == PM_OP_RESUME) {
 		DMSG("Resume to OPP %u", cpu_opp.current_opp);
 
+#if defined(CFG_STM32MP25) || defined(CFG_STM32MP23) || defined(CFG_STM32MP21)
 		/*
 		 * Optimize resume from Stop modes: do not reset
 		 * the OPP if we where on default before suspend.
@@ -705,6 +706,7 @@ static TEE_Result cpu_opp_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint,
 		if (!PM_HINT_IS_STATE(pm_hint, CONTEXT) &&
 		    cpu_opp.current_opp == cpu_opp.default_opp)
 			return TEE_SUCCESS;
+#endif
 
 		return set_opp(cpu_opp.current_opp);
 	}
